      "message": "Is this a TOCTOU here? There would be a small window where host would be able to change `sel-\u003edata_ptr` after `pkvm_host_share_hyp` succeeds but before we assign to `type1`? We should probably memcpy sel and type1 before validating them I guess.\n\nBTW, just a thought. Would it be better to have an api `pkvm_copy_{to,from}_host` that does the same checks in `pkvm_host_share_hyp` and does the copy with host mmu lock held so that we could use it here and avoid unshare at the end? I wanted to implement that for hypercall parameters to overcome the limitation of 10 params for hypercalls(and the complexity in supporting upto 10 parameters)",
